00:03:13.429 --> 00:03:15.470
a session at Next if you
don't have a scattershot

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.264
of other people's logos.

00:03:17.264 --> 00:03:18.680
So you'll see,
these are primarily

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.050
government agencies--
some states, some cities,

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:21.680
some local.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.390
But what you're
really seeing here

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.580
is a list of the public
dataset providers whose data

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.930
we're hosting.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.430
And these are onboarded
and maintained by Googlers

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.320
with inputting
guidance, of course,

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.530
from the subject matter experts
that are the data providers.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.980
And what this really means
is that it's not just

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:43.310
a random collection of data
that someone sticks in an object

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.130
store and never looks at again.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.050
There is a Googler going in
and discovering, finding,

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:51.770
downloading, extracting,
transforming, curating,

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:53.370
and maintaining these datasets.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.150
And we think that provides
a better user experience

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.650
than other public
dataset programs,

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.816
because we are putting the
effort in and the time in

00:03:59.816 --> 00:04:01.700
and our expertise
in the engineering

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.430
to bring these datasets to you.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.532
And so we work closely
with these providers

00:04:06.532 --> 00:04:08.990
to make sure that we understand
what the best practices are

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.095
for them, and that we
can describe the metadata

00:04:11.095 --> 00:04:12.095
as properly as possible.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.334
So we'll just go over some
really high level numbers

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.250
that sound really
impressive, and you guys can

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.458
decide if they mean anything.

00:04:20.458 --> 00:04:24.140
So we've had, in BigQuery
